        "text": "Skip to content\nDonate Today\n# Mark Nagales\nfor San Mateo County\nSupervisor - District 5\nProven Leadership. Trusted Results.\nJoin the Campaign Donate Today\nWatch: Meet Mark Play video: Meet Mark Nagales (opens in a dialog)\nWatch: Meet Mark Play video: Meet Mark Nagales (opens in a dialog)\n## Your Voice for Every Neighborhood.Trusted Across San Mateo County.\n\"Our county faces complex challenges that require steady, practical leadership. I am running to bring a fresh perspective backed by a deep understanding of our community. With a proven track record of building regional coalitions and delivering real solutions, I am ready to lead our district forward on Day One. I would be honored to earn your vote for San Mateo County Supervisor in District 5.\"\nMark Nagales\nMore About Mark\n## We Support Mark Nagales\nJackie Speier\nSan Mateo County Supervisor - District 1\nNoelia Corzo\nSan Mateo County Supervisor - District 2\nRay Mueller\nSan Mateo County Supervisor - District 3\n## Organizations\nSee All Endorsements\n## Leadership that Delivers\nWorking Families\n### Supporting Working Families\nCreated the County's first Guaranteed Basic Income program, launched the regional Economic Advancement Center, and protected tenants.\nChildcare\n### Investing in Childcare\nLed adoption of the County's first Childcare Master Plan and secured $16M to break ground on a new early childhood education center.\nHousing\n### Expanding Local Housing\nLed the effort to earn a state \"housing-friendly\" designation, adopted a 10-year housing master plan, and secured a historic $28M state grant for affordable housing.\nParks & Public Spaces\n### Revitalizing Parks & Public Spaces\nOpened a new 80,000 sq. ft. Library and Parks & Rec campus, built state-of-the-art sports fields and an aquatics center, and expanded free public Wi-Fi.\nPublic Safety\n### Safe Neighborhoods & Healthy Communities\nPartnered with the County on a mental health response pilot program, advanced equity in public safety, and protected youth health.\nTransit\n### Improving Traffic & Transit\nExpanded free neighborhood shuttle routes, delivered over $1M for street safety upgrades, and helped bridge the funding gap for the new Caltrain station.\nRead More",
        "text_limited": false,
        "title": "Mark Nagales for San Mateo County Supervisor — District 5",
        "unresolved_images": []
      }
    }
